+## 2026-10-29 Build31: depth-safe oversized gather completion
+
+**2026-10-29 progress: DONE** bounded clip producer/receipt and current-profile host/Make/guard checks; **NEXT** stream integration followed by target qualification of this dependent slice; **BLOCKED** stream parent integration and SDK/private/console acceptance. No target acceptance is claimed. `codex/world-clip-20261029` is based on the local committed stream-profile repair `4c033a49eb87bb5357d859d82ffebe2e32df03db` (parents `b4cee62b7544704ee09b10759d228401746bf7e7` and current integration `14b5c196db699640f7a9f39bc2318df22dc45ade`). The four owned paths are `port/dreamcast/game/platform/native_static.cpp`, `port/dreamcast/game/world_plan29.mk`, `port/dreamcast/tests/test_world_portal_clip_gather31.py`, and `port/dreamcast/tests/world_portal_clip_gather31/producer_fixture.cpp.in`. The coordinator reviewed this bounded source slice and recorded it locally. GitHub publication is not established. It depends on the stream repair above: hold origin publication/integration until that parent is integrated, then re-synchronize this branch with the fresh integration. The queue, release recipe and global Makefile remain unchanged.
+
+**Exact semantic boundary.** Default-zero `WORLD_PORTAL_CLIP_GATHER31=1` admits only qualified `WORLD_PORTAL_STREAM31=1`, `WORLD_PORTAL_COMPLETION=1`, `SCENERY_CLIP_GATHER=1`, `PS2_PVS_BATCH_COMPOSE=1` and the existing stream/PVS/page parent guards; it requires prefetch, indexed clip, CPU backface, `MESH_CLIP_LEAN` and `MESH_CLIP_ACCEPT` all zero. The emitter's sticky proof is retained only when the actual `clip_strip` is reached by an oversized strip (`count>limit`) and all transformed indices are near/far depth-inside. Near-crossing, capacity-normal clip, culled/empty, partial/reordered/subset/multi-LOD, refused, aborted, unpublished or source-invalid output grants no witness. A depth-inside triangle can contribute at most one emitted triangle, so the existing positive, published, ordered whole-source and `input==output` receipt test proves no triangle was lost. The clipper and sparse gather are unchanged. The bit is per emission, resets on `chunk_restart`, and folds across ordered pages before the existing end-direct/SQ close, page/plan/source/view/material and EF08 receipt checks. There is no general near-clip authority, new receipt, heap/BSS allocation, asset format or pick/page-capacity change.
+
+**Repaired profile gate.** The dedicated fixture now uses the new `stream_portal_profile.py` release-chain reader and the helpers in `test_world_portal_stream_profile31.py`. It compares the clip-absent and explicit-zero primary `native_static.o` command with *both* `MESH_CLIP_LEAN=0` and `MESH_CLIP_ACCEPT=0` explicitly set. The enabled arm adds `SCENERY_CLIP_GATHER=1 WORLD_PORTAL_CLIP_GATHER31=1` and confirms one definition of each, plus the existing stream, portal and render dependencies. The resolved actual chain retains `PVR_PIPELINE=2 PACE_CATCHUP=2 PACE_TRANS_SKIP=4063 PACE_STEADY=1 COARSE=1`; it does not append the old pipeline 1/skip 1 pair. The fixture preprocesses the production `native_static.cpp` early guard using definitions extracted from its actual primary Make command and the literal `src/game/trans.cpp` COARSE/pacing guard using the actual trans command and generated `pace.h`. Current mask 4063 passes; skip 1 is refused by trans; pipeline 1 is refused by Make's steady-pacing guard; catchup 1 is refused by Make. Empty/pattern/multiword/2 clip-control values and unsupported clip compositions are refused. Source-excerpt exact OFF preprocessing and early-guard object identity compare against the new parent `4c033a4`, including the enabled-stream/clip-off control with both alternate clipper controls zero. These excerpt checks are not a full SH-4 object or ELF identity result.
